Preact and htm
--------------
The side panels are rendered with **Preact** (a 3kB alternative to React with the same
modern API) and **htm** (JSX-like syntax in plain tagged template literals, so no
transpiler is needed). Together they let this project keep its no-build-step rule while
still getting real keyed DOM diffing: panels update in place instead of being torn down
and rebuilt, which is what preserves input focus and scroll position. Thank you to
Jason Miller and the Preact contributors.

  Projects: https://github.com/preactjs/preact
            https://github.com/developit/htm
  Homepage: https://preactjs.com
  Versions: preact 10.29.8, htm 3.1.1
  Licence:  Preact - MIT; htm - Apache License 2.0
  Files:    vendor/htm-preact.umd.js
  Licence text: vendor/preact.LICENSE.txt
                vendor/htm.LICENSE.txt

`vendor/htm-preact.umd.js` is an unmodified copy of `htm/preact/standalone.umd.js` from
npm `htm@3.1.1`, which is a prebuilt bundle of preact + preact/hooks + htm exposing the
global `htmPreact`. It is vendored rather than loaded from a CDN for the same reason as
Frappe Gantt: no network requests, works offline.

