Copyright (c) 2018 Jason Miller (htm), Apache License 2.0.


driver.js
---------
The first-run guided tour is **driver.js** by Kamran Ahmed - a dependency-free library
that dims the page, spotlights one element at a time and anchors a popover to it. Nothing
on this page is guessable from looking at it, and pointing at the real control teaches it
far better than a paragraph does. Thank you to Kamran and its contributors.

  Project:  https://github.com/kamranahmedse/driver.js
  Homepage: https://driverjs.com
  Version:  1.8.0
  Licence:  MIT
  Files:    vendor/driver.iife.js
            vendor/driver.css
  Licence text: vendor/driver.LICENSE.txt

Unmodified copies of the `dist` output from npm `driver.js@1.8.0`, vendored rather than
loaded from a CDN for the same reason as the others. Its stylesheet hard-codes colours and
exposes no custom properties for them, so index.html re-skins the popover against this
project's theme tokens.

The two other well-known libraries in this space were ruled out on licensing:
**Shepherd.js** and **intro.js** are both AGPL-3.0, which this MIT project cannot take on
without either relicensing or buying a commercial exception.

